Package: sdpMig2
Type: Package
Title: Stochastic Dynamic Programming Model of Optimal Bird Migration
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Silke", "Bauer", role = "aut"),
    person("Simeon", "Lisovski", role = "aut"),
    person("Martina", "Scacco", email = "martina.scacco@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Stochastic dynamic programming model of optimal migration
    on a network of sites (e.g. hexagons of a grid) between one wintering
    and one breeding site. Daily food gain at each site follows spring
    phenology (growing degree day jerk). Individuals decide each day to
    forage, with an optimal intensity, or to fly to another site, given
    their body condition and the date. Fitness is a terminal reward that
    depends on arrival at the breeding site within an arrival window
    around the local onset of spring and on body condition at arrival.
    The backward iteration computes the optimal policy; the forward
    simulation follows individuals under that policy, with stochastic
    food gain, predation, flight mortality and decision error. The model
    core is written in C++ via 'Rcpp' and 'RcppArmadillo'.
